<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Minerva</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Minerva was the Roman goddess of wisdom, crafts and strategic war, identified with the Greek <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athena">Athena</a>. With Jupiter and Juno she formed the Capitoline Triad worshipped on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/capitoline-hill">Capitol</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. Her cult spread across the empire and was often merged with local deities, as in the temple of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulis-minerva">Sulis Minerva</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bath">Bath</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/minerva.jpg" alt="Minerva" width="320" height="478" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AlMare · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Herculaneum_Collegio_degli_Augustali_Ercole_sull%27Olimpo_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
